#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:80
#: 09f75a7ba5894c90b2c27fdb5ade8157
msgid "The following script is used to change a servo output based on the aircraft's distance from the home position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-lua-scripts.rst:101
#: e78b814ab26a4993b971168e441a083e
msgid "This script begins by defining the update function, which will be called periodically. This function fetches the vehicles current position and home position, and stores them within the local variables current_pos and home. Both of these variables now either hold a Location userdata, or are nil, if the information was not currently available from the vehicle. The variables are then checked to ensure that they were actually provided, before calculating the distance between the locations. After a check to ensure that the distance is never measured as more then 1 kilometer away, the distance is used to set the servo position. The final line in the function is used to reschedule this function to be run again in 1000 milliseconds from the current time. The last line of the script is also used to schedule the function to be run for the first time in 1000 milliseconds from the time at which it's loaded."
msgstr ""

